+`testMatch` picks up every ModuleScript named `*.spec`. Locally, specs run only in Studio, so
+check them with the commands below like any other file.
+
+### CI
+
+`.github/workflows/specs.yml` runs the specs on every pull request. It builds the place from
+`ci.project.json`, uploads it as a Saved version of a dedicated CI place, and runs
+`ci/run-specs.luau` there through the Open Cloud Luau Execution API. The PR fails if any spec
+fails, any suite errors, or no specs are found. The workflow needs these repository secrets:
+`ROBLOX_UNIVERSE_ID`, `ROBLOX_PLACE_ID`, and `ROBLOX_API_KEY`. The API key needs
+`universe-places:write` plus `universe.place.luau-execution-session:read` and `:write` on the
+CI experience.
+
+`ci.project.json` must stay identical to `default.project.json` except for its `name` and
+`ServerScriptService.LoadStringEnabled = true`. Jest needs that property in Open Cloud, and CI
+fails if the two files drift apart, so edit both together.
 
